# CI/CD Pipeline for a Simple Web App

A small Node.js (Express) app with an automated pipeline built using GitHub Actions.

## What the pipeline does
1. Installs dependencies (`npm ci`)
2. Runs tests (Jest + Supertest)
3. Builds a container image and pushes it to GitHub Container Registry
4. Deploys the image to an AWS EC2 server over SSH

## Flow
git push -> test -> docker build -> deploy

## Tech used
Node.js, Express, Jest, Docker/Podman, GitHub Actions, AWS EC2

## Skills practiced
Git, automation, pipelines, build/test flow, secrets management

## Run locally
npm install
npm test
